<title>USA: Heavy rains may disrupt Cuba sugar harvest.</title>
<headline>Heavy rains may disrupt Cuba sugar harvest.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>A tropical disturbance, which may become a tropical depression within the next day or two, in the western Caribbean is bringing heavy rain to the Jamaica, the Cayman Islands and Cuba, private forecaster Weather Services Corp. said.</p>
<p>This would bring heavy rain to Cuba which would disrupt the sugar harvest and possibly threaten crops, it said.</p>
